From 4840df8a80734d50bbeb13243db42eb17eea393e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Chaton <definitelyfrenchname@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 23 Aug 2026 14:56:54 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] cps2w: the QSound sample-bank width fix, gated by a RUNTIME
 profile bit
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Slice D1 of the Vampire Saved MiSTer arc, and the first commit in which
cores/cps2w carries RTL. cores/cps2, cores/cps15 and cores/cps1 stay
BYTE-UNTOUCHED; the diff between the core directories is the trust surface.

THE DEFECT. cores/cps15/hdl/jtcps15_sound.v latches only seven QSound
sample-bank bits (`qsnd_addr[22:16] <= dsp_ab[6:0]`), so DSP sample banks
0x80 and up alias onto 0x00-0x7F and MIS-PLAY existing audio rather than
going silent. The CPS-2 WIDE romset puts its QSound extension in banks
0x80-0x8E.

THE BANK BIT IS dsp_ab[7], MEASURED. The commented-out alternative ordering
left at jtcps15_sound.v:416-417 shows the original author was unsure. MAME's
low-level QSound device settles it: the DSP16A external ROM space is mapped
`map(0x0000,0x7fff).mirror(0x8000)` and the bank latch is
`m_rom_bank = (m_rom_bank & 0x8000U) | offset;` with the sample byte read at
`(u32(m_rom_bank) << 16) | m_rom_offset` — a straight binary bank number in
ab[14:0], no permutation. So widening the latch one bit at a time is correct.

RUNTIME, NOT `ifdef`. The profile is decoded from header byte 41 of the ROM
download (jtcps1_prom_we.v ignores bytes 41-43; its own comment at :52-54
records ten reserved header bytes). ACTIVE LOW, because `[header] fill=0xff`
means an unwritten byte is 0xFF and every stock MRA this core emits must stay
byte-identical to cores/cps2's; jtframe's own JOY_BYTE has the same shape. So
a stock MRA runs jtcps2w.rbf as a stock machine BY CONSTRUCTION.

WHAT IS HERE
  hdl/jtcps2w_profile.v     new — the header-byte decode -> wide_en
  hdl/jtcps2w_qsnd_bank.v   new — the gated bank latch; with wide_en low it
                            is bit-for-bit the stock expression, reset value
                            included
  hdl/jtcps15_sound.v       override — qsnd_addr 23 -> 24 bits, the latch
                            replaced by the module above, new wide_en input
  hdl/jtcps2_game.v         override — 24-bit qsnd_addr, the profile
                            instance, wide_en routed, PCM slot fed
                            qsnd_addr[22:0]
  hdl/pal_lut.hex           the palette brightness LUT, copied verbatim from
                            cores/cps2/hdl and force-added (*.hex is in this
                            repo's .gitignore, which is why a new core can
                            lose it silently). EVERY core that instantiates
                            jtcps1_pal carries its own copy — cps1, cps15 and
                            cps2 all do — because jtframe_ram resolves
                            SYNFILE by bare name and jtsim symlinks
                            $CORES/<core>/hdl/*.hex into the sim directory.
                            Without it the core RENDERS A BLACK SCREEN:
                            $readmemh fails with a warning, the LUT reads
                            back zero and red/green/blue are pinned to 0.
                            Measured on the Verilator lane before the fix:
                            cps2 rendered 12 changed frames in 640 (frame 465
                            mean brightness 146), cps2w rendered exactly one,
                            mean 0.
  cfg/game.yaml             pulls the four .v files from cps2w and drops the
                            two shared originals (jtframe dedups by path, so
                            both copies would otherwise compile)
  cfg/mame2mra.toml         the setname="vsavjw" header row, offset 41 = 0xFE
  ver/game/                 the Verilator sim lane's entry point

PCM_AW STAYS 23, AND THE DESIGN NOTE THAT SAID 24 IS WRONG. jtframe's 8-bit
SDRAM slot cannot be widened past SDRAMW: jtframe_romrq_bcache.v:74
`{SDRAMW-AW{1'b0}}` becomes a replication of -1 at AW=24, SDRAMW=23, which
Verilator rejects outright. That is also why the placement map splits QSound
across two banks instead of growing one slot. Until slice D2 places the
extension, qsnd_addr[23] is produced and gated but not routed; with wide_en
low it is constant 0, so the address the PCM slot sees is bit-for-bit the
reference core's.

MEASURED INERT. cps2 and cps2w run the same stock vsavj download under
Verilator with BIT-IDENTICAL 68k work RAM across 101 consecutive frames, and
with pal_lut.hex in place cps2w reproduces the reference core's match-start
anchor exactly (simulated frame 2502).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01C93kTvSDUfHLL5sbjrArzn
